{#-
Resolves one user-selected span of text into a single world-state snapshot
entry. The audience rules mirror the ones in request-world-state-v2.jinja2,
narrowed to the single entry this prompt returns.
-#}
{# RENDERED CONTEXT (premise, intent, classification, pins, reinforcements, cast) #}
{% set player_character = scene.get_player_character() %}
{% set rendered_context -%}
{% include "extra-context-static.jinja2" %}
<|SECTION:CAST|>
{% if player_character -%}
Player character: {{ player_character.name }}
{% endif -%}
{% if scene.npc_character_names -%}
Other major characters:
{% for npc_name in scene.npc_character_names -%}
- {{ npc_name }}
{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endset %}
{# END RENDERED CONTEXT #}

{# VOLATILE CONTEXT (memory recall + dynamic instructions — placement varies with prompt caching) #}
{% set volatile_context_text %}
{% include "memory-context.jinja2" %}
{% include "extra-context-dynamic.jinja2" %}
{% endset %}
{# END VOLATILE CONTEXT #}

{# THE SELECTION — the message the user selected in, and the span itself.
   `message_text` is the message body as the reader's client renders it, which
   is also the string the host matches the returned mentions against: anything
   quoted from another rendering of the message could never become a
   highlight. #}
{% set selection_text %}
<|SECTION:SELECTED IN|>
{{ message_text }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:SELECTION|>
{{ selection }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endset %}
{# END THE SELECTION #}

{# TRACKED ENTITIES — names already in the snapshot, so an existing entry is
   updated instead of duplicated. #}
{% set tracked_text %}
{% if tracked_entities["characters"] or tracked_entities["items"] or tracked_entities["places"] %}
<|SECTION:ALREADY TRACKED|>
{% for bucket in ["characters", "items", "places"] %}
{% if tracked_entities[bucket] %}
{{ bucket }}: {{ tracked_entities[bucket]|join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}
{% endset %}
{# END TRACKED ENTITIES #}

{% set example_entity = {
    "resolved": true,
    "kind": "item",
    "name": "Auxiliary maintenance locker",
    "snapshot": "What inspecting this entity reveals right now — one to three sentences of concrete fact.",
    "mentions": ["verbatim noun phrase from SELECTED IN"]
} %}
{% if snapshot_audience_context|default(none) %}
{% set example_entity = dict(example_entity, views=audience_views_example) %}
{% endif %}
{% set example_text %}
<|SECTION:EXAMPLE|>
```{{ data_format_type() }}
{%- if data_format_type() == "yaml" %}
{{ yaml({"entity": example_entity}) }}
{%- else %}
{{ {"entity": example_entity} | tojson(indent=4) }}
{%- endif %}
```
A refusal is the same shape with `resolved: false` and no other fields.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endset %}
{# END EXAMPLE #}

{% set audience_context_text %}
{% if snapshot_audience_context|default(none) %}
<|SECTION:ESTABLISHED AUDIENCE KNOWLEDGE|>
{{ snapshot_audience_context | tojson(indent=2) }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}
{% endset %}

{# CUSTOM INSTRUCTIONS — the same user-supplied guidance the refresh pass uses. #}
{% set custom_instructions_text %}
{% if custom_instructions %}
<|SECTION:ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS|>
{{ custom_instructions }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}
{% endset %}
{# END CUSTOM INSTRUCTIONS #}

{# WRITING STYLE (scene-level style guide, if set) #}
{% set writing_style_text %}
{% include "writing-style-instructions.jinja2" %}
{% endset %}
{# END WRITING STYLE #}

{# BROAD HISTORY (budget-aware, includes archive summaries) #}
{% set rendered_context_tokens = count_tokens(rendered_context) %}
{% set volatile_context_tokens = count_tokens(volatile_context_text) %}
{% set selection_text_tokens = count_tokens(selection_text) %}
{% set tracked_text_tokens = count_tokens(tracked_text) %}
{% set example_text_tokens = count_tokens(example_text) %}
{% set audience_context_tokens = count_tokens(audience_context_text) %}
{% set custom_instructions_text_tokens = count_tokens(custom_instructions_text) %}
{% set writing_style_text_tokens = count_tokens(writing_style_text) %}
{% set background_budget = max_tokens - 2500 - rendered_context_tokens - volatile_context_tokens - selection_text_tokens - tracked_text_tokens - example_text_tokens - audience_context_tokens - custom_instructions_text_tokens - writing_style_text_tokens %}
{% set background_history = snapshot_request.context_history(budget=background_budget) if snapshot_request is defined else scene.context_history(budget=background_budget) %}
{% set background_text %}
{% if background_history -%}
<|SECTION:STORY SO FAR|>
{% for line in background_history -%}
{{ line }}
{% endfor -%}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{%- endif %}
{% endset %}
{# END BROAD HISTORY #}

{# RENDER PROMPT #}
{% set volatile_placement = volatile_context_placement() %}
{{ rendered_context }}
{% if volatile_placement != "after_history" %}
{{ volatile_context_text }}
{% endif %}
{{ background_text }}
{{ selection_text }}
{{ tracked_text }}
{{ audience_context_text }}
{% if volatile_placement == "after_history" %}
{{ volatile_context_text }}
{% endif %}
{{ example_text }}
{{ custom_instructions_text }}
{{ writing_style_text }}
<|SECTION:TASK|>
The reader selected the SELECTION inside the message shown in SELECTED IN, asking for it to become a tracked entity in the world state. Resolve that span into exactly one entry.

Decide first whether the selection names a thing at all:
- A person, an object, or a place the selection refers to — resolve it, even when the snapshot pass skipped it and even when the prose barely dwells on it. The reader asked for this one, so the "would a reader learn something new" bar the refresh pass applies does not decide it here.
- Prose that names no distinct entity — a verb phrase, a fragment of dialogue, a mood, a sentence about several things at once — is a refusal. Answer `resolved: false` and nothing else. Do not invent an entity to fill the response.

When you resolve it:
- **`kind`** is exactly one of `character`, `item` or `place`. A person is a character whether or not they act in the scene. A location the scene refers to is a place.
- **`name`** is the reader-friendly title-case name of the entity ("Auxiliary maintenance locker", not "auxiliary_maintenance_locker"). If ALREADY TRACKED lists this same entity, reuse its exact name — your entry replaces it rather than adding a second one.
- **`snapshot`** is one to three sentences of concrete fact about the entity itself — function, history, condition, mechanism, peril, sensory detail. Draw on established context and invent grounded specifics beyond it, but never contradict STORY SO FAR or the message. Metaphor and thematic reading are not facts; describe the thing, not what it means to somebody.
- **`emotion`** is a single word, characters only, and only when the moment supports one. Omit it for items and places.
- **`mentions`** are verbatim noun phrases copied literally from SELECTED IN that refer to this entity, including the selected span when it is one. No pronouns, no possessive bindings ("Elmer's boots" belongs to the boots), no paraphrasing or recasing. These phrases are what the reader's client marks in the message, so a phrase that is not literally in SELECTED IN is dropped.
- **Possessive constructions ("X's Y")** belong to Y. A selection of "Elmer's boots" resolves to the boots.
{% if snapshot_audience_context|default(none) %}

Audience replacements:
- Keep `snapshot`, `emotion`, `name` and `mentions` complete for the reader. Reader-only discoveries and invented flavor remain reader-only.
- Also supply `views`, one assignment for EVERY character in ESTABLISHED AUDIENCE KNOWLEDGE, using only those exact canonical audience names. A ready view has `audience`, `status: ready` and `text`; otherwise use `status: omitted` and `text: null`.
- Each ready `text` is the COMPLETE character-facing replacement, including a safe label and any emotion it conveys. No reader label, emotion or other field is appended to it. Do not copy a secret-bearing name into public text.
- Preserve useful public detail alongside private detail: a bystander's replacement can mention a visible injury while excluding its hidden motive.
- Awareness means knowing the accompanying information, not knowing that an entity exists. Presence, the reader's prose, your own snapshot or a new invented fact do not establish discovery. Use only the supplied stored perspectives and disclosures to support audience content; invent no observation, reaction or belief. Preserve uncertainty and last-known information when current reader truth differs.
- Omit a view when the supplied evidence does not support a useful replacement. Missing or unclassified audiences never receive reader text.
- Do not emit `perspectives`, digests, source references, IDs or provenance; the host attaches the evidence shown above.
{% endif %}

Required response: valid {{ data_format_type() }} matching the example shape — one `entity`, nothing else.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>

## Selected entity
{{ set_data_response(dict(entity={"resolved": true}), cutoff=3) }}
